@biancoresearch Good details above re: Governors' role in oversight of the Fed District Bank presidents. I'd also note how those presidents get chosen in the 1st place.

It's by the Class B & C directors of the regional banks, and Class C directors are appointed by... the Board of Governors in DC, of course. Each bank having 3 Class B directors coming from member banks like Citi & JPM and 3 Class C coming from the Governors that then chose the presidents. 

Hence, the Board of Governors can not only do as @biancoresearch spells out above, but it also has a direct role in appointing half the board members that appoint the presidents.

